#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# NexusBackup disks (Phase 16a/b, docs/hardware.md): disk inventory, SMART, md arrays, and the
# data-array layout (mdadm + XFS) requested from the web UI.
#
#   nexus-disks tick   what nexus-disks.service runs (nexus-disks.timer every 5 minutes, and
#                      nexus-disks.path when the web-api queues a request): handle the queued
#                      requests, finish pending grows, write status.json
#   nexus-disks scan   print the status as JSON (console; changes nothing)
#
# Control directory (default /var/lib/nexus/disks, 2771 root:nexus-webapi, tmpfiles.d/nexus-disks.conf):
#   req-<id>.json  written by the web-api (tmp + rename), at most 4 KiB, consumed (deleted) here:
#                  {"id": <32 hex>, "op": ..., "by": <user>, "quorum_id": <int|null>, ...}
#                  scan                                       re-read everything incl. SMART now
#                  selftest      disk: <serial>, type: short|long
#                  create_array  role: data, level: raid1|raid5|raid6|raid10, disks: [<serial>...]
#                  add_spare     array: <md uuid>, disk: <serial>
#                  replace       array: <md uuid>, disk: <serial>, failed: <serial>|null
#                  grow          array: <md uuid>, disk: <serial>
#                  The destructive ops (create_array, add_spare, replace, grow) are only queued by
#                  the web-api after an approved request with the disk serials typed in; this helper
#                  checks every precondition again (empty disks, never system disks, store empty).
#   status.json    inventory, SMART, arrays, store (0644: the scheduler raises `disk` alerts from it)
#   ops.json       the last operations with their outcome (0644: the scheduler audits them)
#   state.json     arrays waiting for xfs_growfs after a reshape
#
# Roles: system (holds a mounted file system or swap, or is part of an array that does), data /
# metadata (member of the array nexus-data / nexus-metadata), in_use (partitions, signatures, LVM,
# another array), empty (usable for a new array, a spare or a replacement).
#
# The data array: mdadm (metadata 1.2, internal bitmap), XFS with the store's owner and mode set
# by mkfs (protofile), mounted at /var/lib/nexus/chunkstore by a mount unit in /etc/systemd/system
# (bootc keeps /etc; the label comes from the context= mount option). Created only while the store
# holds no files; the scheduler and replicad are stopped around the mount. The metadata role is a
# follow-up (docs/hardware.md): it would move the live catalog, which this helper may not write.
#
# Runs as root in its own SELinux domain (nexus_disks_t): block devices, mdadm, mkfs/xfs_growfs,
# the store's mount unit; no network, never reads keys, the catalog or store contents. Every path
# and tool can be overridden through NEXUS_DISKS_* environment variables (tests). Stdlib only.

